Reduce the duration of the paralysis, or make potions of paralysis rarer
in the game when there are few players in the game. (If you have other
players in your party, they can defend you while you're stuck.)

>You are assuming that NPC's would be implemented in real-time as well.
>I see no reason that you could not implement a multi-user NetHack following
>the same ideas that most muds use... watch for activity on socket connections
>and take action when you see some.  The only Bad Thing you'd have to worry
>about would be what happens while you are paralyzed (and perhaps holding down
>space to skim over your 200 ticks), and another player wanders in?  Of course
>*I* don't see that as a problem <evil grin>.

Of course, you should only have to worry about that if the other player is
of Chaotic alignment. If somebody neutral/lawful should come in and try
and roll you, their god(s) should get pretty pissed.

Hey, here's an idea, if you're paralyzed, you can still think, why lot let
players pray to their god(s) when they're paralyzed for help? I don't
think you can pray while paralyzed in "single-user nethack" now... Spell
casting would be out of the question if the spell required
hand-movements/speech.

